window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["1c"]={"https://theconversation.com/when-it-comes-to-rape-cases-involving-a-celebrity-the-media-too-often-miss-the-point-296256":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"20c37d7fce963f4b84999a53bd6fafc8950ecd89c33328a0592c424bd9eec041","read":"https://theconversation.com/when-it-comes-to-rape-cases-involving-a-celebrity-the-media-too-often-miss-the-point-296256","bytes":178274,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"When it comes to rape cases involving a celebrity, the media too often miss the point","by":[{"n":"Jane Gilmore","r":"PhD candidate, Monash Gender and Family Violence Prevention Hub, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T01:49:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Russell Brand has been convicted of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault and sentenced to ten years and six months in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Age","https://www.theage.com.au/search?isSemanticSearch=true&text=russell+brand"],", ",["The Herald Sun","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/search-results?q=russell%20brand"],", ",["The Guardian","https://www.google.co.uk/search?q=russell+brand&as_sitesearch=www.theguardian.com"],", ",["the ABC","https://www.abc.net.au/news/search?query=russell%20brand"]," and ",["The Australian","https://www.theaustralian.com.au/search-results?q=russell%20brand"]," all reported extensively on the trial, verdict and sentencing. While it’s certainly newsworthy that another public figure has finally been held to account for years of predatory behaviour, the nature of reporting on celebrity rape trials is worth examining."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the ",["UK’s Channel 4","https://www.channel4.com/news/debate-the-use-of-rape-myths-in-trials-must-be-challenged"]," reported, ",["rape myths","https://theconversation.com/rape-myths-shape-how-we-respond-to-sexual-violence-what-are-they-and-what-impact-do-they-have-292594"]," were a frequent and misleading feature in Brand’s trial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Rape myths shape how we respond to sexual violence. What are they and what impact do they have?","https://theconversation.com/rape-myths-shape-how-we-respond-to-sexual-violence-what-are-they-and-what-impact-do-they-have-292594"]]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research","https://global.oup.com/academic/product/reforming-rape-trials-9780198948148?cc=au&lang=en&"]," in Australia has found rape myths are routinely relied on in rape trials, not only by defence lawyers, but also by prosecutors, judges, juries and police."]},{"k":"p","s":["One pervasive rape myth is the “ ",["monster myth","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/14791420.2020.1854802"],"”, the belief that rape is committed by monstrously deviant strangers who attack innocent young girls in public places. ",["Research","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0963947012444217"]," shows this myth is prevalent in media reporting of rape, which has an impact on public perception and acceptance of the monster myth."]},{"k":"p","s":["In reality, as Australian Bureau of Statistics ",["data","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/crime-and-justice/sexual-violence/2021-22#incident-characteristics"]," shows, the person most likely to rape a woman is a man who is her intimate partner."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rape myths in news media"]},{"k":"p","s":["In my research (which has not yet been peer reviewed) I used the AustLii database to identify 32 rape cases in the County Court of Victoria that resulted in a guilty outcome between July 2025 and August 2026. Two of those cases were the ",["Tom Silvagni trial","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-12-11/tom-silvagni-identified-as-man-found-guilty-of-rape/106129488"]," and the ",["Ralph Carr trial","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-25/ralph-carr-sentenced-to-six-years-jail-for-rape/107074230"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I also searched for news reporting on those trials, finding 198 articles that fit the inclusion criteria. Between them, Silvagni and Carr received 85% of the media coverage of the entire dataset."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rape myths were present in almost 45% of the headlines in the dataset. They appeared in more than 60% of the non-celebrity cases (almost entirely centred on the monster myth) and just over 40% of the celebrity cases (where the myths that women commonly lie about rape and that men charged with rape are an object of pity predominated). Every publication in the study included rape myths in some of their headlines about rape trials."]},{"k":"p","s":["In other words, if media are reporting on a celebrity trial, too often the celebrity becomes the story, not the rape or the victim-survivor."]},{"k":"p","s":["If they’re reporting on rape cases, the monster myth is more likely to appear in the headline than the facts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of the 32 cases I identified, 13 were cases of rape in a family and domestic violence (FDV) context. Less than 3% of the articles were about the cases involving rape in an FDV context."]},{"k":"p","s":["Journalists cannot identify the complainant (the legal term for the victim-survivor) in a rape trial, so if they report an FDV related rape case, they often cannot name the perpetrator because it can identify the victim-survivor."]},{"k":"p","s":["The courts often use pseudonyms for both people when they publish sentencing remarks. Journalists could report these cases using those pseudonyms, preserving the victim-survivor’s anonymity while still informing the public about the rape. I could not find a single article in my dataset that did this."]},{"k":"p","s":["Focusing such breathless attention on celebrity cases and the rare stranger-danger rape endorses exactly the kind of monster myths that ",["The Guardian","https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/nov/10/judge-sentenced-russell-brand-praised-rape-myths-justice-bennathan"]," yesterday praised the judge in Brand’s trial for dispelling in his sentencing remarks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Suppression orders and the principles of open justice"]},{"k":"p","s":["In both the Silvagni and Carr cases, the men involved had been granted suppression orders that prevented media identifying them before they were convicted."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Age","https://www.theage.com.au/national/victoria/everybody-hates-you-every-single-day-why-the-silvagni-case-is-the-tip-of-the-iceberg-20260302-p5o6mg.html"],", the ",["Herald Sun","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/justin-quill-how-the-rich-like-tom-silvagni-exploit-a-legal-loophole-to-buy-court-secrecy/news-story/0bd936c84e4d3ef3ce4647c23b0836eb"],", ",["The Guardian","https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/jul/31/melbourne-businessman-guilty-rape-identity-suppression-gag-order-open-justice-ntwnfb"],", ",["The Australian","https://www.theaustralian.com.au/subscribe/news/1/?sourceCode=TAWEB_WRE170_a_GGL&dest=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theaustralian.com.au%2Fcommentary%2Feditorials%2Fkeeping-secrets-a-bad-thing-for-our-open-society%2Fnews-story%2F3abd45ffd480e2ba633f5433802ec04a&memtype=anonymous&mode=premium&v21=HIGH-Segment-2-SCORE&V21spcbehaviour=appendend"]," and the ",["ABC","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-03/victoria-media-suppression-orders-court-reporting/106406950"]," all published editorials or opinion pieces on the principles of open justice and how suppression orders prevented journalists reporting on the functioning of criminal courts, an essential component of journalists’ role of keeping the public informed about the functions of a democratic society."]},{"k":"p","s":["The media cannot claim to be serving the principles of open justice and ride a wave of their own self-righteous anger at suppression orders when those orders do not prevent them covering the trial. Particularly when they are failing to cover so many trials that do not feature a well-known perpetrator."]},{"k":"p","s":["The celebrity is not the story. The rape is the story. The victim survivor and the effect he had on her life is the story. The structures that allowed him to commit his crimes can be the story, but breathless sensationalism has no place in reporting on rape."]}],"chars":4532},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"b2e4326c532e45099918e3c5d1463b779ac413a2233983e88178cfe2dbea38cd","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/chile","bytes":86209,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Chile travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T15:05:46+00:00","mod":"2026-11-09T12:06:58+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice page also covers Rapa Nui (Easter Island)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. If you have onward travel plans within the region, check travel advice for all destinations you plan to travel through. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Chile’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Chile set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Chilean Embassy in the UK","https://www.chile.gob.cl/reino-unido/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport should have an ‘expiry date’ after the day you plan to leave Chile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Chilean dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["British-Chilean dual nationals must enter and leave Chile using their Chilean passport. Chilean entry and exit requirements for dual nationals may change without notice. For further information check with the ",["Chilean Embassy in the UK","https://www.chile.gob.cl/en/reino-unido/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Chile for up to 90 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Chilean immigration authorities will give you a tourist card (‘tarjeta de turismo’), an A5-sized white form. Keep it safe and give it to immigration when you leave the country. If you lose it, Chilean police investigations (PDI) allows you to ",["request a copy online","https://pdivirtual.cerofilas.gob.cl/etapas/ver/31401667/0"]," (choose ‘Duplicado de tarjeta de turismo’). You can also go to the nearest PDI office."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer (to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons), you must ",["meet the Chilean Government’s entry requirements","https://serviciomigraciones.cl/en/home/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chile requires children travelling with only one parent, with a guardian or alone, to have permission from the non-travelling parent or parents. Parents travelling with children for tourism have faced difficulty leaving Chile at the end of their visit when only one parent is present. You must have"]},{"k":"li","s":["a written notarised authorisation from the non-travelling parent(s)"]},{"k":"li","s":["an original birth certificate"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling with children aged 17 and under, check the website of the ",["Chilean Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://www.chile.gob.cl/en/chile/xplica/ingreso-y-salida-de-menores-del-pais"]," (website in Spanish) for what documents you need to show."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with dual national children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before a dual national child aged 17 or under leaves Chile, you must get authorisation to travel from a Chilean notary (‘notaría’) if the child is travelling:"]},{"k":"li","s":["alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["with only one parent or guardian"]},{"k":"li","s":["with friends or relatives"]},{"k":"p","s":["If a child was born in Chile, they must have a Chilean passport to leave the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling to Rapa Nui (Easter Island)"]},{"k":"p","s":["To ",["enter Rapa Nui (Easter Island)","https://www.gob.cl/rapanuiprotegida/en/requirements/"]," you must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["complete a ",["Rapa Nui entry form","https://ingresorapanui.interior.gob.cl/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a reservation registered with ",["SERNATUR, the national tourism service","https://serviciosturisticos.sernatur.cl/"]," (select region ‘Valparaiso’ and comuna ‘Rapa Nui’ to refine your search for accommodation) or an invitation letter from the provincial delegation"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Chile guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Chile","https://www.aduana.cl/aduana/site/edic/base/port/viajero_turista.html"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Chile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Chile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some individuals or groups claiming to represent the interests of indigenous communities have carried out attacks in the Araucanía, Biobío and Los Ríos regions of the country. State actors and businesses operating in these regions are the primary targets of these groups. You should exercise caution and follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anarchist groups have also carried out attacks, mostly in the Santiago Metropolitan region. Attacks are principally aimed at causing property damage. Keep bags with you at all times, as unattended bags might be treated with suspicion by local authorities. Report any suspicious behaviour or unattended packages to local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violent protest in Santiago and other Chilean cities, particularly on Friday afternoons and evenings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even peaceful protests can become violent. The largest protests usually take place in central Santiago. Police can use tear gas and water cannons against protesters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all demonstrations. Under Chilean law, you can be deported if you’re involved in or promote violent acts that could disturb social order or the system of government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nationwide protests often take place on significant dates, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["11 September (anniversary of the military coup)"]},{"k":"li","s":["29 March (Day of the Young Combatant)"]},{"k":"li","s":["1 May (Workers’ Day)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing, mugging and thefts from vehicles are very common throughout Chile, including inside airports, churches, hotels and bus stations, and at viewpoints and petrol stations."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is a list of scams and techniques which have been used on British Nationals in Chile, especially in central Santiago and Valparaiso:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Distraction robbery: The victim is distracted by one person while a second person steals the victim’s handbag or backpack from their chair or from under the table."]},{"k":"li","s":["Liquid spill: Liquid is ‘accidentally’ spilled on a traveller, and the scammer steals the victim’s valuables while pretending to be assisting cleaning it off."]},{"k":"li","s":["Tyre puncture: The driver pulls over owing to a punctured tyre (not knowing that their tyre has been deliberately punctured). A person then approaches the car offering to help, and distracts the driver whilst a second person steals belongings from the car."]},{"k":"li","s":["Hire cars: Hire cars are targeted and broken into whilst parked at a viewpoint, petrol station or other location. Sometimes the driver is approached and distracted by one person while belongings are stolen from the car by a second person."]},{"k":"li","s":["Airport taxi: Unlicenced taxi drivers at Santiago Airport add extra digits to the amount for the taxi journey i.e. charging 5,000,000 CLP (approx. 5,000 GBP / 5,000 USD) instead of 50,000 CLP. Others have convinced passengers to enter their pin number into a credit card reader whose display cannot be read. People have lost up to 10,000 GBP via this method."]},{"k":"li","s":["Theft of belongings at Santiago airport: This includes luggage stolen both before check-in at the airport terminal and from the baggage carousel after arrival."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxi scams at Santiago Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many foreign visitors have been scammed for large amounts of money by unlicensed taxi drivers, including in airport taxis. Well-known taxi companies can be booked via ridesharing apps. Only book and pay for official taxis from inside the airport before exiting the building."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not use any transport from inside the airport if you cannot pay for it before getting into the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to recognise official taxis","https://www.mtt.gob.cl/viaja-seguro-en-taxis.html"]," (in Spanish) and be wary of people impersonating authorised taxi drivers. There are criminals inside the airport arrival area who dress up as authorised taxi drivers, including people inside the airport arrival hall wearing official-looking lanyards and jackets, with printed price lists."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce the risk of being overcharged you can insist on paying in advance for your journey at one of the two official taxi booths in the arrivals at Santiago’s international airport, immediately after customs and just before you head through to the public area of arrivals. If one of the booths does not have a card reader available on that day, then you can go to the other booth instead."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do decide to pay in the taxi, you should insist on seeing the amount you are charged before you present your card for payment at the end of the journey. Carefully review the amount being charged on portable credit card machines before paying, including the number of zeroes shown on the screen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a taxi takes you to an ATM to withdraw cash for payment, do not let the driver near the ATM while you use it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read information about the official transportation options at Santiago airport:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["taxis","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=taxis"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["buses","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=buses"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["transfers","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=transfer"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["car rental","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=arriendo-vehiculos"]," (read the section ‘Vehicle crime’ below if you are planning on renting a car)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Book taxis in advance rather than hailing one from the street, especially late at night. Keep in groups and avoid walking alone late at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your valuables and passport somewhere secure, such as in a hotel safe. Bags hanging on chairs or mobile phones on tables can be targeted by thieves, who may use distraction techniques or work in pairs. Take particular care:"]},{"k":"li","s":["around tourist sites, and areas popular with tourists"]},{"k":"li","s":["in cafes and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["at transport hubs, including at the airport, bus stations and ports"]},{"k":"li","s":["in hotel lobbies during arrival and departure"]},{"k":"li","s":["in service (petrol) stations and service station restaurants"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by bus or coach, take care of your belongings when getting on and off. Keep your valuables with you, do not put them in storage compartments, especially for long journeys between regions. Be extremely wary of distractions at bus stations, where there are frequent thefts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent theft (muggings)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Muggings happen frequently, especially in Santiago and Valparaiso, and increasingly with weapons such as guns and knives. Muggings can take place during the day and in plain sight of others. Be aware of your surroundings, particularly in tourist areas or near official buildings. Muggers will target:"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourists"]},{"k":"li","s":["people carrying large amounts of money – leaving ATMs or currency exchanges, for example"]},{"k":"li","s":["your passport (carrying a photocopy is enough)"]},{"k":"li","s":["valuable watches or jewellery"]},{"k":"li","s":["your mobile phone"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not resist any attempted mugging."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in criminals:"]},{"k":"li","s":["targeting rental cars in major cities – they puncture the car’s tyres, often while at traffic lights, distract the occupants when they notice the tyres and steal valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["following people from the airport on arrival and robbing them, sometimes at gunpoint"]},{"k":"li","s":["targeting vehicles entering or leaving private residences while the gates are opening or closing"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying out carjacking’s in Santiago, especially in affluent areas – some armed carjackers target high-end vehicles on highways"]},{"k":"li","s":["targeting people parked at viewpoints and stealing belongings from their cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings in and around the airport, when driving and on arrival at your destination. Keep vehicle doors locked and windows closed. Wait for gates to fully close before leaving your vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re robbed, hand over your cash and valuables without resistance. If you’re carjacked, local authorities say it is best to raise your hands and get out of the vehicle to avoid violence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["People have been given ‘spiked’ drinks in nightclubs and bars, particularly in the Suecia and Bellavista areas of Santiago. These incidents leave victims open to theft or assault. Keep your drinks in sight and be wary of people offering to buy drinks for you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry a printed copy of the photo page of your passport with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to drink alcohol in public places including streets, roads, squares and promenades."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Using or possessing drugs is illegal and can lead to prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal in Chile and are increasingly widely accepted socially, although much of Chilean society is conservative."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fires in national parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Open fires are illegal in national parks in Chile, outside permitted camping areas. Local authorities may revoke your tourist permit if you’re caught starting a fire in a Chilean national park. You may be asked to leave the country voluntarily within 72 hours or face deportation. If your open fire starts a larger forest fire, you may also face criminal penalties and fines."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to go exploring or mountaineering, tell the local authorities before you set off. For further information on mountaineering, contact the ",["Federación de Andinismo de Chile","https://marmolejo.feach.cl/"],". For any other type of exploring, contact the ",["Chilean Embassy in London","https://www.chile.gob.cl/en/reino-unido/en"]," to see if you need a permit. The rescue services in Chile are good, but you may have to pay if they help you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Chile for 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have your passport and proof of your tourist status, such as your tourist card (‘tarjeta de turismo’) or the entry stamp in your passport, with you in the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information about driving licences in Chile","https://www.transporteinforma.cl/atencion-de-usuarios/preguntas-frecuentes/preguntas-licencias-de-conducir/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hire a car, get appropriate insurance. Windscreen repair can be expensive, so consider including windscreen damage cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot get car insurance if you’re driving on Rapa Nui (Easter Island). If you have an accident or do any damage to your vehicle there, you’ll have to pay for the repairs yourself."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Main roads in Chile are surfaced, but you may need a 4-wheel drive vehicle in the countryside. Be prepared for a range of driving conditions, from snow and ice to hot sandy deserts. Between June and September, winter weather sometimes temporarily closes the Chile-Argentina border crossing high in the Andes, including the main Los Libertadores crossing between Santiago and Mendoza."]},{"k":"p","s":["Toll roads are increasingly common."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmine accidents mainly affect livestock and local people crossing borders at unauthorised points. Most minefields are near the borders with Peru and Bolivia in the extreme north of Chile (regions XV, I and II) and Argentina in the south (region XII). Although most minefields are clearly marked, some signs and fences are old and damaged and may be hard to spot. In some cases, minefields are laid right up to the edge of highways. Check with local authorities before travelling to more rural areas, stick to clearly marked roads and observe all warning signs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"]," for information about how to prepare, and how to react if there is a warning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Heavy rain and flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["When necessary, the Chilean National Service for Disaster Prevention and Response (SENAPRED) issues warnings for heavy rain which may impact travel plans. Road conditions may be hazardous, with increased risk of delays and accidents. If you travel, plan your journey carefully and allow extra time. Follow local news, weather updates and the ",["SENAPRED website","https://senapred.cl/informate/eventos"]," (in Spanish) for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chile often has severe forest fires which can be very destructive and spread rapidly. These fires have caused multiple deaths, as well as sometimes causing the closure of national parks and roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you find yourself in or near the affected areas of any fires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities, including evacuation orders"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media to stay informed of the rapidly evolving situation"]},{"k":"li","s":["notify friends and family of your safety"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your personal security plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["make evacuation plans that do not rely on British government assistance"]},{"k":"li","s":["have travel documents up to date and easily accessible"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry identification at all times, such as your passport or a copy of it"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Major earthquakes are a risk in Chile. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],". Take note of instructions in hotel rooms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Building regulations require new structures to take account of earthquake risks. Safety measures are widely known and put into practice by national organisations and the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["A chain of volcanoes is active in the Puyehue and Los Lagos region (500 miles south of Santiago). There is a continuing risk of eruptions in Chaiten in southern Chile, Llaima in the Conguillo National Park and Lascar in northern Chile. Copahue, a volcano on the Argentina-Chile border, erupts periodically, causing local residents to be evacuated. Villarrica, a volcano near the popular tourist destinations of Pucon and Villarrica in the IX region of La Araucanía, is also active."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to these areas, monitor local media reports and follow ",["local authority volcano monitoring advice","https://www.sernageomin.cl/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Chile. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Araucanía Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is ongoing civil unrest in the Araucanía Region, especially around Temuco. This includes attacks by groups of demonstrators against both people and property. Be cautious if you travel within the Araucanía Region. There is an ongoing state of emergency in the provinces of Biobío, Arauco, Cautín and Malleco because of a significant increase in violent incidents. The military are assisting regional police. Follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 131 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["recommended vaccinations for Chile","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," or ",["Easter Island","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/69/chile-easter-island#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Chile","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile"],", including altitude sickness, which is a risk in parts of Chile. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are confirmed cases of dengue fever on Rapa Nui (Easter Island). Take steps to avoid being bitten by mosquitoes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hantavirus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hantavirus is present in Chile. Read more information about ",["Hantavirus in Chile on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile#Outbreaks"],". Further guidance on Hantavirus is available from the ",["UK Health Security Agency","https://ukhsa.blog.gov.uk/2026/05/05/what-is-hantavirus-how-is-it-transmitted-and-what-are-the-symptoms/"]," and ",["Chile’s Ministry of Health","https://www.minsal.cl/ministerio-de-salud-declara-alerta-sanitaria-por-hantavirus-desde-atacama-a-magallanes/"]," (website in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Chile"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are good health facilities in Santiago and other major cities, but private clinics and hospitals are expensive. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is only one hospital on Rapa Nui (Easter Island) and its facilities are limited. People suffering from serious illnesses or injuries are taken by air ambulance to mainland Chile for treatment. Make sure your travel insurance covers this."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chile-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-2"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-chile-guidance"]," if you’re living in Chile."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Chile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 131"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 132"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 133"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Chile"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Chile"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Chile"]," in Chile"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chile-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chile-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/chile/british-embassy-santiago"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-chile"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":22722,"change":"Removal of information about heavy rain and severe mudslides in eastern Santiago ('Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"f6e863996b102882d47309753f994dd3e3ea490af897b0e312efcc6bbe36ba8b","read":"https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005","bytes":184342,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ethiopia’s peace deal is unravelling – what went wrong with the Tigray agreement","by":[{"n":"Alemayehu Fentaw Weldemariam","r":"Ph.D. Fellow, Center for Constitutional Democracy, Indiana University"}],"pub":"2026-09-29T08:37:09Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Pretoria peace deal","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"]," in Ethiopia was an agreement to cease hostilities. It wasn’t a comprehensive political settlement. A ",["political settlement","https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780192848932.003.0002"]," is an enduring agreement among powerful groups that delivers some benefits to avert conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ethiopian government and the Tigray People’s Liberation Front signed the Pretoria agreement in 2022. It ",["stopped large-scale fighting","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-tigray-war-parties-agree-pause-expert-insights-into-two-years-of-devastating-conflict-193636"]," in Tigray and created a framework for disarmament and other immediate measures. But it was also meant to pave the way for political dialogue addressing underlying disputes."]},{"k":"p","s":["This political settlement would have restored Tigray’s self-rule through an elected regional government. It would have restored the region’s representation in ",["Ethiopia’s two houses of parliament","https://theconversation.com/what-is-federalism-why-ethiopia-uses-this-system-of-government-and-why-its-not-perfect-217217"],", and the federal executive and judiciary. Instead, the Tigray People’s Liberation Front was ",["deregistered and Tigray was excluded","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn0pngz2rego"]," from the June 2026 elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Pretoria deal","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"]," also required the withdrawal of Eritrean and other non-federal forces from Tigrayan territories. It called for accountability for alleged war crimes and other violations."]},{"k":"p","s":["This broader settlement was never reached. The ",["consequences","https://acleddata.com/expert-comment/ethiopia-conflict-expert-insights"]," are now becoming clear."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fighting has ",["resumed","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/26/is-ethiopia-on-the-verge-of-another-civil-war-as-fighting-erupts-in-tigray"]," between government troops and Tigrayan forces, with air and drone strikes hitting the region. Seven armed organisations – including groups that fought one another during the ",["2020-2022 Tigray war","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/conflict-ethiopia"]," – have formed an ",["alliance","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/seven-ethiopian-armed-groups-announce-anti-government-alliance-2026-09-21/"]," seeking to remove Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed’s government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the international response to the escalation in conflict has focused on the ",["Tigray People’s Liberation Front","https://www.britannica.com/place/Tigray-historical-region-Ethiopia#ref248314"],". In late September 2026, for instance, US ambassador Ervin Massinga ",["accused","https://et.usembassy.gov/statement-on-recent-developments-in-tigray-and-afar/"]," the front of making the"]},{"k":"p","s":["poor decision to launch a large-scale offensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["He described the campaign as an “ ",["unwinnable fight","https://et.usembassy.gov/statement-on-recent-developments-in-tigray-and-afar/"],"”, and threatened further sanctions against the front and leaders of the newly formed armed alliance."]},{"k":"p","s":["But focusing on who launched the latest offensive risks obscuring a more important question: why the ",["peace process","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-tigray-war-parties-agree-pause-expert-insights-into-two-years-of-devastating-conflict-193636"]," that ended the Tigray war in 2022 failed to prevent a return to conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a ",["constitutional scholar and country expert","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=arlPf30AAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"]," on Ethiopia, whose focus includes peacemaking and peacebuilding. In my view, the failure to move from the Pretoria agreement to a broader political settlement has had three major consequences:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the emergence of an armed alliance connecting conflicts across several regions"]},{"k":"li","s":["renewed attacks that risk further civilian casualties and mass displacement"]},{"k":"li","s":["growing tensions with Eritrea that could draw Ethiopia’s conflicts into a wider regional confrontation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preventing a broader war in Ethiopia will, therefore, require more than a return to the Pretoria agreement. The country needs a comprehensive political settlement. This should be negotiated between Abiy’s leadership and anti-government forces – not just another bilateral agreement with Tigray."]},{"k":"h","s":["The transition"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Pretoria agreement","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"]," imposed military and political obligations on both the Ethiopian government and Tigrayan forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tigray People’s Liberation Front was to disarm. The federal government was to help remove the front’s terrorist designation, restore essential services in Tigray and enable humanitarian access. Federal authority was to return to Tigray."]},{"k":"p","s":["Subsequent ",["peace talks in Nairobi","https://www.peaceagreements.org/media/documents/ag2464_6391cad1825da.pdf"]," linked the handover of Tigray’s heavy weapons to the withdrawal of foreign and non-federal forces from Tigray."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia’s troubled history provides clues to why an all-out civil war is possible","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-troubled-history-provides-clues-to-why-an-all-out-civil-war-is-possible-149648"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Tigrayan forces began surrendering heavy weapons in January 2023. An African Union monitoring team ",["witnessed and confirmed","https://apnews.com/article/2214ccbe43c96047f9f8f9465da9a988"]," this process. But the federal government did not secure the corresponding withdrawal of forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["These failures don’t absolve Tigray’s leadership of some responsibility for the escalation in conflict. Its restoration of the ",["pre-war regional administration","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/tigray-party-restores-pre-war-government-threat-northern-ethiopia-peace-2026-05-05/"]," went against the Pretoria agreement, which provided for an interim administration established through dialogue. It would govern until elections could be held under the supervision of the National Election Board. Further, reports of ",["forced military mobilisation","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/07/06/ethiopia-tigray-authorities-forcibly-recruiting-civilians"]," are serious."]},{"k":"p","s":["But these actions occurred within a peace process already weakened by incomplete implementation."]},{"k":"h","s":["The consequences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The formation of an ",["anti-government coalition","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckp84pj8zpngo"]," changes the environment. The Ethiopian Peoples’ Forces Alliance for Survival includes the Tigray People’s Liberation Front, the Oromo Liberation Army, Amhara Fano elements and organisations from other regions. Some of these groups previously fought one another."]},{"k":"p","s":["The alliance doesn’t mean Abiy’s government is about to collapse. The federal state ",["retains","https://www.theafricareport.com/431885/can-abiys-drones-give-him-the-upper-hand-in-ethiopias-full-blown-war/"]," the army, air power, drones, federal revenues and the machinery of government."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the alliance doesn’t need a common ideology or unified battlefield command to create problems for the federal government. Coordination of operations across regions could be enough."]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in Tigray could draw federal forces northward. Fighting in ",["Amhara","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-amhara-people-are-being-portrayed-as-the-enemy-the-dangerous-history-of-ethnic-politics-212626"]," might absorb forces and obstruct access to the north. Pressure in ",["Oromia","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-other-conflict-whats-driving-the-violence-in-oromia-187035"]," might require the government to defend approaches to the capital and major transport corridors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Each front can, therefore, affect the others even if the alliance’s forces never fight side by side."]},{"k":"p","s":["The immediate challenge for the federal government is the dispersion of forces across distant conflicts with different terrain, supply lines and political dynamics."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Renewed air and drone attacks","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cry8zwwq21pxo"]," raise the danger of another humanitarian crisis, too. Tigray is ",["still recovering","https://theconversation.com/starvation-as-a-weapon-of-war-how-ethiopia-created-a-famine-in-tigray-268395"]," from the 2020-2022 war. Escalation risks civilian casualties, displacement and disruption to humanitarian assistance."]},{"k":"h","s":["The Eritrea and Sudan question"]},{"k":"p","s":["Eritrea’s role in the latest escalation in conflict remains disputed. Ethiopia ",["accuses","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/ethiopia-accuses-eritrea-military-aggression-backing-armed-groups-2026-02-08/"]," Asmara of supporting armed groups. Eritrea ",["denies","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn87lzrj1l7o"]," it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Abiy and other senior Ethiopian officials have also repeatedly said they must have ",["access to the Red Sea","https://adf-magazine.com/2026/02/eritrea-ethiopia-port-dispute-heats-up/"],". Talk of the ",["Eritrean port of Assab","https://www.dw.com/en/port-assab-becomes-flashpoint-for-ethiopiaeritrea-relations/a-75453946"]," has been understood in Eritrea as a threat. Assab is part of Eritrea’s internationally recognised territory. Any attempt to acquire it by force would violate Eritrean sovereignty."]},{"k":"p","s":["The conflict could also become entangled with Sudan’s war. According to a ",["Reuters report","https://www.reuters.com/investigations/ethiopia-builds-secret-camp-train-sudan-rsf-fighters-sources-say-2026-02-10/"],", Ethiopia hosts a camp used to train paramilitary fighters for Sudan’s Rapid Support Forces. Ethiopia has denied involvement. It instead accuses Sudan’s armed forces of ",["supporting","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/28/ethiopia-accuses-sudan-egypt-of-backing-tigray-rebels-as-fighting-rages"]," the Tigray People’s Liberation Front. Sudan ",["denies","https://addisstandard.com/sudan-army-rejects-ethiopias-claims-of-backing-armed-opposition-coalition/"]," this."]},{"k":"p","s":["If these alignments harden, the Ethiopian and Sudanese conflicts could provide one another with weapons supply routes. They could also supply recruits, rear bases and external support. This raises the risk of conflict extending from Sudan through northern Ethiopia towards Eritrea and the Red Sea."]},{"k":"h","s":["What next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The immediate priorities are ending attacks on populated areas and protecting humanitarian corridors. Independent monitoring must also be restored and outstanding security obligations completed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another bilateral bargain between Addis Ababa and the Tigray People’s Liberation Front would be inadequate. The conflict now connects armed movements and political grievances across several regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preventing a wider war requires a comprehensive agreement that involves the federal government, the alliance of armed groups, non-armed political actors and civil society. It must address territorial disputes, political representation, elections, accountability, regional autonomy, constitutional reform and the distribution of power."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pretoria stopped one phase of one war. Its incomplete implementation left unresolved disputes that are now colliding."]}],"chars":7600},"https://theconversation.com/international-surrogacy-and-the-narrow-legal-idea-of-what-makes-a-family-legitimate-295302":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"bf0648582d32fc9ee87497d9c1ba048815e1e5bc153454c19a2c4a2f6023657c","read":"https://theconversation.com/international-surrogacy-and-the-narrow-legal-idea-of-what-makes-a-family-legitimate-295302","bytes":179481,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"International surrogacy and the narrow legal idea of what makes a family legitimate","by":[{"n":"Katie Tonkiss","r":"Senior Lecturer in Sociology, Aston University"}],"pub":"2026-11-04T14:37:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A recent family court judgment in the UK highlighted ethical issues with the practice of international surrogacy. The case is thought to be the first to come before a court in the UK involving a surrogate who gave birth in China, where surrogacy is illegal. It raised numerous concerns – including about the welfare of the surrogate and child, the use of sex selection and the child’s immigration status and nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Surrogacy","https://theconversation.com/topics/surrogacy-4090"]," is a growing practice in the UK, with the number of ",["births doubling","https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/19/rise-overseas-surrogates-increases-risk-stateless-babies-experts-warn"]," between 2015 and 2025. Most of these babies are born overseas through ",["international surrogacy","https://www.ngalaw.co.uk/numbers-talk-our-scope-of-surrogacy"],". In the UK, surrogacy is permitted only under altruistic circumstances (such as a relative or friend of the intended parents carrying the baby, with no payment beyond expenses). This can make it difficult to find a domestic surrogate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Domestic surrogacy ",["is prohibited","https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2025/769508/EPRS_BRI(2025)769508_EN.pdf"]," across all EU member nations. But in countries such as Georgia, Ukraine and many states in the US, commercial surrogacy – where the surrogate receives payment over and above her expenses – is legal. An industry has grown around the practice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depending on their place of birth, babies born through international surrogacy can enter a legal grey area where their nationality is uncertain. In some cases, this can lead to the risk of statelessness because of discrepancies in how legal parenthood – and therefore often nationality – are recognised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where commercial surrogacy is legal, a surrogate may not be recognised as having legal parenthood of a child at all. But when a family seeks to return to their country of residence with the child, if surrogacy is not legal in that country, then the legal parenthood of the “intended parents” may also not be recognised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Given that legal parenthood determines nationality in most countries, this can leave children born through surrogacy without a clear claim to nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["the case","https://caselaw.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ewfc/2026/279"]," of the baby born in China, it was not until the child was 20 months old that the parenthood of the “intended parents”, and therefore the child’s British nationality, was established in law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attempts to increase regulation of surrogacy internationally ",["have stalled","https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/19/rise-overseas-surrogates-increases-risk-stateless-babies-experts-warn"]," because of disagreement between states over the ethical issues raised by the practice. But having no nationality, as can arise in international surrogacy, also calls into question the foundations upon which access to legal identity at birth is built."]},{"k":"p","s":["For my ",["new book","https://manchesteruniversitypress.co.uk/9781526183514/"],", I researched cases of international surrogacy across Europe and North America, speaking to parents as well as surrogates. I found that ideas about what counts as a “legitimate” family shape decisions about what citizenship, if any, a child should have at birth."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is a ‘legitimate’ family?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The idea of “legitimate” and “illegitimate” families has become almost obsolete in other areas of the law. But it persists when it comes to establishing nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":["In European countries, nationality at birth is decided by the parent or parents’ nationality. The child effectively inherits it from the parents. A number of ",["high-profile cases","https://www.echr.coe.int/documents/d/echr/fs_surrogacy_eng"]," before the European Court of Human Rights have sought to ensure that no child born through surrogacy could be rendered stateless, despite the prohibition of the practice across EU member states."]},{"k":"p","s":["But I found that despite this, decisions about legal parenthood – and therefore nationality – continue to be shaped by gendered assumptions about what counts as parenthood. Specifically, the need for a gestating mother and a father who is biologically related to the child is central. I also found that, even where countries have laws to protect children born through surrogacy, LGBTQ+ parents may face obstacles in registering births, because of the absence of a gestational mother in the paperwork."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the US, nationality typically is decided by birth on US soil. However, in cases of international surrogacy – where the child is born overseas – a child may inherit their citizenship from a parent who is a US citizen."]},{"k":"p","s":["A series of ",["cases","https://immigrationequality.org/andrew-elad-and-ethan-dvash-banks/"]," before the US Supreme Court showed how stricter standards were applied to the children of LGBTQ+ couples born through international surrogacy. They were assumed to be born “out of wedlock”, despite their parents being married."]},{"k":"p","s":["These children struggled to obtain US nationality as a result. The court ruled to prevent this discrimination, but this work has reinforced the importance of marriage to parenthood. That is, it focused on the legitimacy of the marriages, rather than the relevance of marriage to parenthood."]},{"k":"p","s":["While ethical debates around surrogacy are unlikely to be resolved any time soon, children continue to face the risk of statelessness."]},{"k":"p","s":["States that oppose surrogacy argue that strict rules are needed to prevent exploitation, the commodification of children and human trafficking. These concerns are very real. Yet growing numbers of children are being born through international surrogacy and face the risk of statelessness."]},{"k":"p","s":["Addressing this requires not only renewed efforts at regulation, but also a fundamental rethink of nationality laws. So often, these tie a child’s legal identity to narrow ideas of what counts as a “legitimate” family."]}],"chars":5138},"https://theconversation.com/gibrans-exit-leaves-prabowo-with-expanding-power-and-indonesia-with-questions-296698":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"a95285161cb2c749e673045677aec47227d3a04f8bbd0e0ac572c819df78d736","read":"https://theconversation.com/gibrans-exit-leaves-prabowo-with-expanding-power-and-indonesia-with-questions-296698","bytes":179929,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Gibran’s exit leaves Prabowo with expanding power—and Indonesia with questions","by":[{"n":"Puteri Atikah","r":"Dosen, Universitas Negeri Medan"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T09:41:49Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Gibran Rakabuming Raka’s resignation as Indonesia’s vice president on Thursday, November 12, 2026, marks more than an end to a political controversy. It could remove the last major obstacle to President Prabowo Subianto’s efforts to consolidate power and bring Indonesia’s political system under tighter presidential control."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gibran submitted his resignation to Prabowo and the leadership of the People’s Consultative Assembly (MPR) shortly before the House of Representatives (DPR) was scheduled to consider invoking its right to state an opinion (Hak Menyatakan Pendapat, or HMP), a procedure that could lead to impeachment."]},{"k":"p","s":["The move ",["followed a Supreme Court ruling","https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/indonesia-vp-gibran-hands-his-resignation-upper-house-2026-11-12/"]," annulling his high school equivalency certificate, which he had used to qualify for the 2024 vice presidential election. The day before he resigned, 120 lawmakers from all eight parliamentary factions had backed the HMP motion. After his resignation, ",["the DPR cancelled its plenary session","https://en.antaranews.com/news/442003/gibran-officially-resigns-hmp-plenary-meeting-canceled"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gibran’s departure leaves Prabowo without a rival power centre within the executive, at least until a replacement vice president is elected. More importantly, it weakens the political network of former president Joko “Jokowi” Widodo, whose influence helped bring Prabowo to power in 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["With seven of the eight parties in parliament backing Prabowo’s coalition, the president has greater room to concentrate political and state resources in his own hands."]},{"k":"h","s":["From oligarchic rivalry to presidential dominance"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Prabowo–Gibran partnership underscored the pragmatism of coalitions among Indonesia’s political parties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prabowo had twice lost presidential elections to Jokowi before joining his cabinet as defence minister in October 2019. Prabowo’s eventual partnership with Gibran was made possible by a ",["Constitutional Court decision","https://www.mkri.id/perkara/persidangan/putusan?page=78&perPage=20"],", which allowed candidates under 40 to run for president or vice president if they had held elected office."]},{"k":"p","s":["Issued under Chief Justice Anwar Usman, Jokowi’s brother-in-law and Gibran’s uncle, the ruling triggered accusations of political nepotism and earned the court the nickname “Family Court.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jokowi’s political influence was built on substantial public support. Indikator Politik Indonesia’s ",["October 2024 survey","https://indikator.co.id/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/RILIS-INDIKATOR__04-OKTOBER-2024.pdf"]," found that 74.96 percent of respondents remained satisfied with his performance shortly before he left office. This popularity helped Prabowo and Gibran secure their electoral victory."]},{"k":"p","s":["But their alliance was never built on shared political interests. Once Prabowo assumed office, the two camps began competing for control over political networks, bureaucratic positions and state resources. Gibran’s frequent public appearances and distribution of aid, reminiscent of Jokowi’s populist style, also raised speculation that he was positioning himself for the 2029 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Without a political party of his own, however, Gibran had limited leverage. Prabowo gradually weakened the networks associated with his predecessor. He removed National Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo, a longtime Jokowi loyalist, in an effort to loosen Jokowi’s hold over the police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier, Erick Thohir, a former Jokowi ally who had led the state-owned enterprises ministry, was moved to the youth and sports portfolio in September 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["The creation of Danantara—which consolidated Indonesia’s state-owned enterprise assets—further eroded Jokowi’s influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["This rivalry reflects what political sociologists Vedi Hadiz and Richard Robison ",["observed in 2004","https://books.google.com/books/about/Reorganising_Power_in_Indonesia.html?id=N_yVrHF6--4C"],": Suharto’s fall did not dismantle Indonesia’s oligarchy but merely allowed it to reorganise within democratic institutions. Political competition thus became a struggle among rival elites for state power and economic resources."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jeffrey Winters makes a related argument in his book, ",["Oligarchy (2011)","https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/oligarchy/5CC556B4483F7F3FDE1CADF928C04671"],", examining how concentrated wealth enables elites to protect and extend their political power."]},{"k":"p","s":["From this perspective, Gibran’s resignation is not simply the defeat of one political figure. It represents another stage in the redistribution of power within Indonesia’s oligarchy, this time increasingly toward Prabowo."]},{"k":"h","s":["The architecture of centralized power"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prabowo’s efforts to centralise authority extend well beyond his political rivalry with Jokowi. His flagship programs, including Free Nutritious Meals (MBG), Red and White Village Cooperatives and People’s Schools, require substantial funding and coordination from the central government. They also expand the state’s presence in local communities, creating new channels through which the administration can exercise influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The growing involvement of the Indonesian Military (TNI) in civilian programs adds another dimension. Military personnel have been deployed to support MBG kitchens, accelerate the construction of village cooperatives and instil discipline among students at People’s Schools. This blurs the boundaries between civilian administration and military responsibilities, potentially strengthening the president’s reach into everyday governance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Danantara also offers another instrument for consolidating control. Unlike Jokowi, who relied heavily on state-owned enterprises to drive ",["infrastructure development","https://press.umich.edu/Books/R/Ruling-Indonesia3"],", Prabowo has established a centralised structure for managing their assets. According to the ",["International Monetary Fund’s 2025 report","https://www.elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/002/2026/010/article-A001-en.xml"],", Danantara consolidates state-owned enterprises under one entity, with both Danantara and the new state-owned enterprise regulatory body reporting directly to the president. This gives the administration considerable influence over state capital and investment decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fiscal policy has moves in a similar direction. The central government’s cuts to regional fiscal transfers have placed local administrations under pressure, prompting 18 governors from the ",["Association of Indonesian Provincial Governments (APPSI)","https://www.jakartadaily.id/local/16216055131/18-governors-urge-indonesias-finance-minister-to-reverse-regional-budget-cuts"]," to protest to the finance minister against the cuts."]},{"k":"p","s":["As ",["The Jakarta Post reported in October 2025","https://www.thejakartapost.com/business/2025/10/12/regional-dissent-boils-over-as-fiscal-transfer-cuts-bite"],", the proposed reductions threatened regional budgets already heavily dependent on central government funding. The dispute highlights the limits of Indonesia’s decentralisation Indonesia has pursued since the 1998 Reformasi, which has never fully translated into meaningful regional autonomy."]},{"k":"p","s":["This concentration of authority builds on a process that began under Jokowi. His administration expanded presidential influence over political institutions and state resources, creating a model of governance that Prabowo can now take further."]},{"k":"p","s":["The rivalry between the two presidents was therefore less a clash between opposing visions of power than a struggle over who would control the machinery of the state."]},{"k":"h","s":["What comes next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prabowo’s position is now stronger, but greater control does not necessarily mean greater political stability. The weakening of Jokowi’s network may settle one elite rivalry, but competition over access to state resources could generate new conflicts within Prabowo’s own coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["More importantly, centralising power also concentrates political responsibility. As economic uncertainty deepens and ",["public dissatisfaction grows","https://en.tempo.co/read/2121411/survey-75-of-indonesians-feel-stressed-by-government-policies"],", Prabowo will have fewer political intermediaries to absorb criticism or share the blame for government failures."]},{"k":"p","s":["His administration will therefore face a fundamental choice: open up political space for criticism and democratic accountability, or tighten control over dissent to protect its authority. The government’s tendency to label critics “foreign lackeys” (antek asing), arrest protesters and expand the military’s role in civilian affairs suggests that the latter approach may prevail."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gibran’s resignation marks Prabowo’s consolidation of power. This signals Reformasi’s end: democratic institutions survive, yet power is recentralising around elites never dismantled after 1998. The question is no longer who governs, but how far Prabowo will go to silence challengers."]}],"chars":7776},"https://theconversation.com/berhenti-atau-diberhentikan-buntunya-politik-wapres-gibran-di-tengah-polemik-ijazah-296339":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"9bf558b99c39d43c94278c441396a9f188cbba2d95f86967ae7d44cf5f5918a2","read":"https://theconversation.com/berhenti-atau-diberhentikan-buntunya-politik-wapres-gibran-di-tengah-polemik-ijazah-296339","bytes":180822,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Berhenti atau diberhentikan? Buntunya politik Wapres Gibran di tengah polemik ijazah","by":[{"n":"Aditya Rahmadhony","r":"Peneliti Pusat Riset Hukum, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T04:39:35Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Putusan MK dan MA memperbesar pertanyaan tentang keabsahan dokumen pendidikan Gibran."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Dukungan politik melemah, sementara DPR mulai membuka jalan Hak Menyatakan Pendapat."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Krisis kepercayaan publik mempersempit pilihan Gibran: mundur atau menghadapi pemakzulan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wakil Presiden Gibran Rakabuming Raka kini menghadapi situasi yang semakin sulit. Persoalan ijazah yang semula tampak seperti sengketa administratif telah berkembang menjadi krisis hukum, politik, sekaligus kepercayaan publik. Jalan untuk bertahan semakin sempit, sementara mundur pun bukan keputusan tanpa konsekuensi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 10 November 2026, Gibran dilaporkan ",["menyampaikan niat mengundurkan diri","https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/fate-indonesias-vice-president-hangs-balance-lawmakers-mull-probe-2026-11-10/"]," kepada Presiden Prabowo Subianto. Namun, ia juga meminta kesempatan untuk membuktikan keabsahan dokumen pendidikannya melalui proses hukum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perkembangan ini menunjukkan bahwa Gibran berada dalam posisi dilematis: bertahan dengan risiko tekanan yang semakin besar atau berhenti sebelum proses pemberhentian melalui mekanisme konstitusional bergulir lebih jauh."]},{"k":"p","s":["Setidaknya ada tiga pukulan yang membuat ruang geraknya semakin sempit: hukum, politik, dan sosial."]},{"k":"h","s":["1. Persoalan hukum yang belum sepenuhnya terjawab"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 6 Oktober 2026, Mahkamah Konstitusi (MK) melalui ",["Putusan Nomor 01/PHPU.PRES-XXIV/2026","https://s.mkri.id/public/content/persidangan/putusan/putusan_mkri_15075_1791296266.pdf"]," menyatakan permohonan yang mempersoalkan persyaratan pendidikan Gibran tidak dapat diterima. Alasannya, para pemohon tidak memiliki kedudukan hukum (legal standing) untuk mengajukan perkara tersebut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, ada ",["catatan penting","https://www.mkri.id/berita/mk-tidak-menemukan-bukti-ijazah-sma-gibran-atau-sederajat-25893"]," dalam pertimbangan hukum MK. Mahkamah menyatakan tidak menemukan bukti meyakinkan bahwa Gibran memiliki ijazah, sertifikat, atau diploma pendidikan luar negeri yang dapat dijadikan dasar penyetaraan dengan pendidikan setingkat SMA. MK juga menyerahkan penilaian terhadap keabsahan bukti-bukti tersebut ke lembaga lain yang memiliki kewenangan sesuai UUD 1945."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Bisakah kita memakzulkan Wapres Gibran?","https://theconversation.com/bisakah-kita-memakzulkan-wapres-gibran-255430"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 30 Oktober 2026, Mahkamah Agung (MA) melalui ",["Putusan Nomor 742 K/TUN/2026","https://putusan3.mahkamahagung.go.id/direktori/putusan/11f1dcce1102fda0b396313331353033.html"]," mengabulkan kasasi dan menyatakan Surat Keterangan Penyetaraan Pendidikan SMA atas nama Gibran ",["tidak sah dan batal demi hukum","https://news.detik.com/berita/d-8746999/ini-putusan-lengkap-ma-batalkan-suket-ijazah-sma-gibran"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua putusan tersebut tidak otomatis membatalkan pengangkatan Gibran sebagai wakil presiden. Namun, pembatalan dokumen yang digunakan untuk memenuhi persyaratan pencalonan menimbulkan pertanyaan serius: bagaimana negara memastikan bahwa persyaratan seorang pejabat publik benar-benar terpenuhi?"]},{"k":"h","s":["2. Dukungan politik yang tak lagi pasti"]},{"k":"p","s":["Polemik ini mulai bergerak dari tekanan di luar pemerintahan menuju arena politik formal. Ketua DPR Puan Maharani pada 10 November ",["mengonfirmasi","https://www.dpr.go.id/kegiatan-dpr/berita/Puan-Usulan-Hak-Menyatakan-Pendapat-Ikuti-Mekanisme-Konstitusi-70488"]," bahwa pimpinan DPR telah menerima laporan mengenai pengumpulan tanda tangan anggota dewan untuk mengusulkan Hak Menyatakan Pendapat. Usulan tersebut akan diproses sesuai mekanisme konstitusi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Memang, belum ada keputusan DPR untuk memulai proses pemakzulan. Namun, ketika persoalan ini mulai masuk ke agenda resmi parlemen, tekanan terhadap Gibran tidak lagi bisa dianggap sebatas riuh di media sosial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di tengah dinamika tersebut, muncul pula spekulasi mengenai ketegangan antara lingkaran politik Prabowo dan mantan Presiden Joko Widodo. Situasi ini memperlihatkan bahwa dukungan politik dalam koalisi tidak selalu permanen. Ketika seorang pejabat dianggap membawa beban politik, kepentingan partai dan koalisi dapat berubah."]},{"k":"h","s":["3. Krisis kepercayaan sosial paling sulit dipulihkan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan Gibran telah menyentuh pertanyaan mendasar tentang keadilan: apakah standar yang berlaku bagi pejabat negara juga berlaku bagi masyarakat biasa?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi masyarakat, ijazah bukan sekadar dokumen administratif. Seseorang yang melamar pekerjaan harus menunjukkan ijazah. Mereka yang ingin melanjutkan pendidikan harus memenuhi persyaratan yang ditetapkan. Kesalahan dokumen bahkan dapat membuat seseorang kehilangan kesempatan kerja atau pendidikan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, ketika dokumen pendidikan seorang wakil presiden dipersoalkan dan surat penyetaraannya kemudian dinyatakan tidak sah oleh MA, masyarakat wajar mempertanyakan konsistensi penerapan aturan. Persoalannya bukan sekadar apakah Gibran memiliki pendidikan yang cukup, melainkan apakah prosedur yang berlaku telah dijalankan secara benar dan setara."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian Tom R. Tyler tentang psikologi legitimasi","https://doi.org/10.1207/s15327957pspr0104_4"]," menjelaskan bahwa penerimaan masyarakat terhadap otoritas tidak hanya ditentukan oleh kekuasaan atau hasil keputusan, tetapi juga oleh persepsi bahwa proses yang ditempuh berlangsung adil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Gibran dan politikus muda lain yang lahir dari dinasti politik: pedang bermata dua bagi demokrasi","https://theconversation.com/gibran-dan-politikus-muda-lain-yang-lahir-dari-dinasti-politik-pedang-bermata-dua-bagi-demokrasi-125720"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Sementara itu, ",["riset tahun 2024 mengenai kepercayaan terhadap institusi politik di Indonesia","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpoleco.2024.102572"]," menunjukkan bahwa situasi politik, termasuk tingkat konflik dan permusuhan selama proses politik, turut memengaruhi kepercayaan masyarakat terhadap institusi negara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Artinya, polemik Gibran tidak berdiri sendiri, tetapi berlangsung di tengah persoalan kepercayaan masyarakat terhadap institusi dan penegakan hukum. Ketika masyarakat melihat adanya kemungkinan perlakuan berbeda bagi mereka yang memiliki kekuasaan, dampaknya bukan hanya terhadap citra seorang wakil presiden, melainkan juga anggapan bahwa hukum tak berlaku setara bagi semua orang."]},{"k":"h","s":["Berhenti sebelum dimundurkan?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemberhentian presiden dan wakil presiden diatur dalam Pasal 7A dan 7B UUD 1945. Ada enam kategori alasan pemberhentian, mulai dari pengkhianatan terhadap negara, korupsi, penyuapan, tindak pidana berat lainnya, perbuatan tercela, hingga tidak lagi memenuhi syarat sebagai presiden dan/atau wakil presiden."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prosesnya panjang. DPR harus terlebih dahulu menyatakan pendapat dalam rapat paripurna dengan dukungan sekurang-kurangnya dua pertiga anggota yang hadir, dengan kuorum minimal dua pertiga dari seluruh anggota DPR. Pendapat tersebut kemudian diperiksa MK, yang wajib memutus paling lama 90 hari."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika MK ",["membenarkan pendapat DPR","https://www.mkri.id/public/content/pmk/PMK_PMK_21.pdf"],", proses berlanjut ke DPR dan MPR untuk memutuskan pemberhentian."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan demikian, pemakzulan bukan proses otomatis. Persoalan pembatalan dokumen penyetaraan pendidikan juga masih harus diuji implikasi konstitusionalnya terhadap persyaratan jabatan wakil presiden."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di sisi lain, Pasal 8 ayat (2) UUD 1945 mengatur bahwa jika wakil presiden berhenti, MPR harus bersidang paling lambat 60 hari untuk memilih penggantinya. MPR memilih wakil presiden dari dua calon yang diajukan oleh presiden."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam situasi ini, berhenti mungkin menjadi pilihan politik yang lebih baik daripada membiarkan krisis legitimasi terus berlarut-larut. Namun, pengunduran diri bukan berarti pengakuan otomatis atas pelanggaran hukum, apalagi menghapus kewajiban untuk mempertanggungjawabkan persoalan administratif yang telah muncul."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ujian etika bagi pejabat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan Gibran bukan hanya tentang kemampuan mempertahankan jabatan, tetapi juga tentang etika seorang pejabat publik dalam menghadapi krisis kepercayaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jabatan wakil presiden bukan sekadar hasil kemenangan pemilu atau legitimasi formal konstitusi. Jabatan ini membawa tanggung jawab untuk menjaga kepercayaan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika jalur hukum belum memberikan jalan keluar yang meyakinkan, dukungan politik semakin tidak pasti, dan kepercayaan publik terus tergerus, Gibran menghadapi pilihan yang semakin terbatas. Terlebih posisinya tidak terlepas dari putusan kontroversial MK Nomor 90/PUU-XXI/2023 yang mengubah syarat calon wakil presiden kemudian memuluskannya ke pucuk pemerintahan. Apakah bertahan masih merupakan pilihan terbaik?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Patut ditunggu di mana titik akhirnya, apakah pilihannya mengundurkan diri (berhenti) atau diberhentikan dari jabatannya sebagai wakil presiden? Dalam situasi seperti ini, keberanian untuk berhenti mungkin justru menjadi ujian terbesar bagi seorang negarawan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Politik itu penuh negosiasi, tetapi etika dan legitimasi harga mati","https://theconversation.com/politik-itu-penuh-negosiasi-tetapi-etika-dan-legitimasi-harga-mati-223333"]]}],"chars":7710},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kiribati":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"949b3baea002e323f524c5b8f0d43c14b69e6ec6139835425486ede03a409a01","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kiribati","bytes":39240,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kiribati travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:02:38+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kiribati/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Kiribati’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Kiribati set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Fiji High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kiribati, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Kiribati without a visa for up to one month."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must hold a ticket for return or onward travel and enough funds for your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities will normally grant you a one-month stay on arrival. You can apply for one-month extensions, up to a maximum of 3 extra months, from the ",["Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Immigration","https://www.mfa.gov.ki/immigration/"]," in Bairiki. Your passport must remain valid to extend your stay."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must pay a 20 Australian dollar departure tax at the airport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Kiribati. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a strict quarantine regime for importing food, plant and animal (including fish) products to Kiribati. For further information, contact:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Biosecurity Services SPC-Plant Protection Service Private Mail Bag Suva, Fiji Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Phone: (679) 3370 733 Fax: (679) 3370 021 Email: pps@spc.int"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking Kiribati handicrafts to Australia or New Zealand"]},{"k":"p","s":["Strict Australian or New Zealand import regulations may apply to some Kiribati handicrafts, including straw products and shells. Check ",["Australia travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/entry-requirements"]," and ",["New Zealand travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/new-zealand/entry-requirements"]," for details. You can get a phyto-sanitary certificate in Kiribati, but the customs authorities may still confiscate items."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Kiribati"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Kiribati, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always be able to show an official form of ID such as your passport. The police will usually accept a printed copy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession or trafficking of drugs is a serious offence in Kiribati, and prison sentences may be heavy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public nudity"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should respect local customs about dress, including swimming costumes. Local laws ban public nudity and revealing swimming costumes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual acts are illegal. If found guilty, the penalty could be up to 14 years imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Internet and phone services"]},{"k":"p","s":["Internet and mobile phone services are available in some parts of Kiribati. Not all of the outer islands are connected. Services can be unreliable and expensive because of the country’s remote location."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stray dogs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stray dogs have bitten visitors. Be cautious, particularly on the beach. If a dog approaches you, do not run. Reaching down as if to pick up something off the ground can be enough to scare dogs away. If a dog bites you, seek medical attention immediately."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Very few places accept credit cards in Kiribati. There are ATMs at branches of the Bank of Kiribati and ANZ in Betio, Bairiki and Bikenibeu on Tarawa atoll."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and boating safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not swim in the lagoon in south Tarawa, as it is highly polluted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take great care when swimming in the sea around Kiribati. There are very strong rip tides along coast and reef areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always wear safety equipment during boating trips. Squalls can happen at very short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Kiribati, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Kiribati. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions are poor on Tarawa, but driving standards are reasonable. Minibuses can be dangerously overloaded."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the wet season, which normally runs from November to April, there can be strong winds and sea swells. Flooding and coastal inundation can cause disruption to essential services and infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor regional and international weather updates from the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/sp/"],", the Fiji Meteorological Service and local newspapers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Droughts"]},{"k":"p","s":["There can be severe droughts in Kiribati. The authorities may put water restrictions in place."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 994 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Kiribati","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/118/kiribati#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Kiribati","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/118/kiribati#General_Information"],", including Dengue."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink and use only boiled or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks. Do not eat local shellfish or lagoon fish on Tarawa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Kiribati"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities at the general hospital in Tarawa are modest. Elsewhere, nurse practitioners generally staff clinics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmaceuticals – both prescription and non-prescription medicines – are generally not available. Bring any medicines you need with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need any non-basic medical treatment, you will usually need medical evacuation from Kiribati. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover evacuation by air ambulance plus the cost of medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Kiribati"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone 999 (ambulance, fire, police) or local numbers:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 994"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 993"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 992"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/kiribati/british-high-commission-suva"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kiribati/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":10365,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/namibia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"95bca61d258f6647f24c83c36d99371093c992770fbd7b250c582eb91d2af13a","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/namibia","bytes":55506,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Namibia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-10T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:15:46+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/namibia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Namibia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Namibia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Namibian High Commission in the UK","https://www.namibiahc.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Namibia, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive. It must also have at least 3 blank pages. If you’re travelling to Namibia through South Africa read the ",["South Africa travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-africa"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 1 April 2025 you will need a visa to visit Namibia. The Namibian authorities have launched a visa on arrival scheme, which is extended to UK passport holders."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can either apply for a visa on arrival when you arrive at a Port of Entry for Namibia, or you can apply online before you travel for an e-visa. For either route, the cost is 1,600 Namibian dollars for travellers over 11 years old. Children between the ages of 11 to 6 will will be charged 800 Namibian dollars. Children under the age of 6 will not be charged a fee for a visa on arrival. When granted a visa on arrival, you will receive a multiple entry visa valid for the period that you have requested."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to work or volunteer, or if you want to stay longer, you must apply for the appropriate visa. These categories are not covered by the visa on arrival process."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa on arrival"]},{"k":"p","s":["Full details on how to apply for the online e-Visa for Visa on Arrival, including the online application form, can be found at ",["Visa On Arrival","https://eservices.mhaiss.gov.na/visaonarrival"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This link also includes information on the process for the application and the documentation required."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for other visa categories"]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply through the ",["Namibian High Commission in the UK","https://www.namibiahc.org.uk/services-for-foreign-nationals.php"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the date on your entry stamp and the amount of time you have been given to stay is correct. Immigration officials will check these details when you leave Namibia."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Namibian authorities could detain, arrest or fine you if you overstay or have an incorrect or missing entry stamp in your passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children aged 17 and under"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a parent travelling with children aged 17 and under, you must carry their:"]},{"k":"li","s":["valid passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["full birth certificate with both parents’ details (original or certified copy)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Namibian immigration officials will not accept an abridged (short) birth certificate. If your child was born in the UK, you can ",["order a full unabridged birth certificate online","https://www.gov.uk/order-copy-birth-death-marriage-certificate"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a legal guardian and your name is not on the birth certificate, you will need to have documentation to prove it."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re not a parent or legal guardian of children you’re travelling with, you must have an affidavit from their parents or guardians giving consent."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a child is travelling with one parent or legal guardian, the other parent or legal guardian should give consent for travel in an affidavit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unaccompanied children must carry:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a valid passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of consent from a parent or legal guardian in an affidavit"]},{"k":"li","s":["a letter from their host giving the address where they’ll be staying"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the Namibian High Commission in the UK for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with children through a South African airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling with children through a South African airport, see ",["South Africa travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-africa/entry-requirements"]," for information about the documents you must carry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Namibia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Namibia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/157/namibia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Namibia","https://www.namra.org.na/customs-excise/page/customs-procedure-travellers-guide-information"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Namibia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Namibia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Muggers often target tourists in Windhoek. Attacks may be violent and can take place at any time of day and in busy city-centre locations. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of your surroundings, especially after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your valuables and cash out of sight or use a hotel safe"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not change large sums of money in busy public areas"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Gangs sometimes try to enter vehicles at busy intersections in Windhoek. Theft from vehicles, particularly at service stations, is common. To reduce the risks:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave your vehicle unattended at fuel stops"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep car doors locked and windows shut, especially in heavy traffic"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep valuables off the seats and out of sight"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce the risk of robberies from taxis:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not hail taxis from the street, particularly in Windhoek"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your hotel, guest house or tour operator to recommend a reputable taxi company"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not enter townships at night, unless you are with someone with local knowledge"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Credit card skimming"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases of credit card skimming at some hotels and lodges. Always keep your card in sight when paying and check your statement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry UK photo ID. You may need to show ID at police checkpoints in Windhoek and other major towns and cities. Keep copies of the photo page of your passport and important documents separately in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are not illegal in Namibia. Certain same-sex sexual acts are illegal, but generally not prosecuted. There are no laws against discrimination on the grounds of sexual orientation. Conservative attitudes towards LGBT+ individuals remain, especially in rural regions. Showing affection in public may result in unwanted attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for using or smuggling illegal drugs can be severe. Penalties include large fines and imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. You will be prosecuted and could get a fine or prison sentence for buying or trafficking these goods, including ivory and rhino horn."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police have detained people for taking pictures of the President’s official residence. Check before taking photographs of government buildings or in secure areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your travel insurance covers you for any adventure activities you plan to do, like quad biking, dune boarding or hot air ballooning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Namibia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have your valid UK photocard driving licence with you in the car."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take out comprehensive insurance as accidents are common on gravel and dirt roads. If you’re planning to hire a car, check what insurance cover is provided. Most policies will not cover accidents that do not involve other vehicles or animals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the rainy season from January to April, many gravel roads deteriorate. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not go faster than 80 km/h"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry 2 spare tyres for punctures"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry plenty of water"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the road conditions before setting off"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid driving at night outside towns, as wildlife and livestock are serious hazards"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 211111 (in Windhoek) or 10111 (everywhere else) and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Namibia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/157/namibia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Namibia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/157/namibia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Namibia. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namibia’s hot and dry climate can cause skin problems and dehydration. Make sure you carry a good supply of drinkable water."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namibia has one of the highest prevalence rates of HIV in the world. In 2021 the UNAIDS Report on the Global AIDS Epidemic estimated that around 210,000 adults aged 15 or over were living with HIV. This was around 11.8% of the adult population, compared to around 0.2% of adults in the UK. Take normal precautions to avoid exposure to HIV/AIDS."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Namibia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are good medical facilities in Windhoek. Private hospitals may insist on payment before starting treatment even if you have comprehensive travel insurance. They may ask you to pay and reclaim from your insurer later. Some travel insurance policies are not recognised by some Namibian hospitals. Check if your product is accepted in Namibia before you travel and get alternative coverage, if needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Namibia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/namibia-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Namibia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 10111, 999, 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Namibia"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Namibia"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Namibia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/namibia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/namibia/british-high-commission-windhoek"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/namibia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Namibia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-namibia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":13173,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"17c1d6db5d86049d216fffc4b26ecf14e70fb3e7dcb6a5bae2f9a93721e7f422","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/thailand","bytes":98820,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Thailand travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-12T10:20:34+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"h","s":["Thailand-Malaysia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to parts of the south, near the Thailand-Malaysia border:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Pattani Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yala Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["Narathiwat Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["The districts of Chana, Thepa, Na Thawi and Saba Yoi in southern Songkhla Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO also advises against all but essential travel on the Hat Yai to Padang Besar train line that runs through these provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to regular attacks in the provinces by the border with Malaysia. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Thailand-Cambodia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the land border with Cambodia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fighting occurred along parts of the border in July 2025, and further clashes took place in early December, involving rocket and artillery fire. Land borders and crossings between Thailand and Cambodia remain suspended. Tourist sites close to the border, including the Khao Phra Wihan Preah Vihear temple, the Ta Kwai Ta Krabey temple and the Ta Muen Thom Tamone Thom temple, are closed. There are unexploded landmines in the area. Travel to affected border regions should be avoided."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":["If you have been impacted by travel disruption and need to review your Thai Visa, please follow the guidance published by the Thai Immigration Bureau: ",["Immigration Bureau Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/100068925981064/posts/1222102076763980/?mibextid=wwXIfr&rdid=eOHccV0J1ePRNu9N"]]},{"k":"h","s":["It is illegal to carry cannabis out of Thailand"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have been caught carrying cannabis out of Thailand, including while transiting through other countries. Many international airports have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items, which may be used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers. If caught you will be arrested or fined."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Thailand set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Thai Embassy in the UK","https://london.thaiembassy.org/en/index"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Thailand, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and have at least 1 blank page."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a dual national, it is best to leave Thailand on the same passport you used to enter – this will avoid problems at immigration."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 15 September 2026, if you enter Thailand under the visa exemption scheme, you can stay for up to 30 days for tourism only. Visa-exempt entry does not cover business travel, including attending conferences, meetings or other business activities. If you are travelling for business purposes, you should obtain the appropriate visa before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Visa-exempt entry for tourism through land-border immigration checkpoints is normally limited to 2 entries per calendar year. This restriction does not generally apply to arrivals by air. If you frequently enter Thailand as a tourist, immigration officials may ask for evidence of your onward travel, accommodation, or sufficient funds, and may refuse entry if they believe you are not a genuine visitor."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you entered Thailand before 15 September 2026, you will usually be allowed to stay for the period granted when you arrived. If you want to stay longer, you must get the appropriate visa before you travel or, if eligible, apply for an extension through the Thai immigration authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be asked to show that you meet the entry requirements. This could include proof that you have enough money for your stay (at least 10,000 Thai baht per person or 20,000 Thai baht per family) and evidence of onward or return travel. British nationals have been refused entry for failing to provide this evidence."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your permission to stay in Thailand, you could be fined, detained, deported or banned from re-entering the country. Make sure you understand the conditions of your stay and get any visa extension you need before your permission expires."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to work, study, retire or live in Thailand, you must get the appropriate visa before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Digital Arrival Card"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 1 May 2025, all foreign nationals entering Thailand, whether by air, land or sea must complete a digital arrival card online before arrival. Travellers can ",["register for an arrival card","https://tdac.immigration.go.th/"]," within 3 days before they arrive."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overstaying your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay the period of your visa, you will get a fine of 500 Thai baht a day up to a maximum of 20,000 baht. You risk being:"]},{"k":"li","s":["held in detention"]},{"k":"li","s":["deported at your own expense"]},{"k":"li","s":["banned from re-entering Thailand for up to 10 years"]},{"k":"p","s":["Conditions in detention centres can be harsh."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Thailand, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Thailand guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/221/thailand#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a public health measure, Thailand has introduced health screening for travellers arriving from affected regions. ",["Travellers are subject to a mandatory quarantine or self-isolation period of at least 21 days","https://x.com/prdthailand/status/2059480037406191802?s=46"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Thailand","https://www.customs.go.th/list_strc_simple_neted.php?ini_content=individual_160503_03_160905_01&lang=en&left_menu=menu_individual_submenu_01_160421_01"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking cigarettes into Thailand"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take more than 200 cigarettes per person into Thailand. This is enforced at customs on arrival. If you go over the limit, you could be fined 10 times the value. Your cigarettes will likely be confiscated."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Thailand","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Thailand"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Thailand."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular terrorist attacks in the 4 provinces in the southern tip of Thailand by the border with Malaysia. The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) advises against all but essential travel to these provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Martial law is in place in most areas in these provinces, which means security forces have greater security enforcement and investigative powers. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, terrorist attacks could take place anywhere in Thailand. Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in tourist destinations. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Targets might include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["security forces"]},{"k":"li","s":["government offices"]},{"k":"li","s":["locations popular with tourists and foreigners"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["shops and supermarkets"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport infrastructure"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation can be unpredictable and has led to periods of civil and political unrest. Avoid protests, political gatherings, demonstrations and marches."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry your valuables and cash securely to guard against pickpocketing"]},{"k":"li","s":["beware of bag-snatchers, especially on motorbikes"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when travelling in open transport like tuk-tuks"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid sleeping on buses and trains – people have had items taken from bags while asleep"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not hand your passport over as a guarantee, for example to motorcycle or jet-ski rental businesses. Companies may hold on to passports against claimed damage."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crime, including gun crime, rarely involves tourists. However, several foreign nationals were victims of gun violence in Bangkok in 2018. Take care when travelling in unfamiliar areas and avoid walking through isolated areas alone, especially at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent sexual assaults and unprovoked attacks can happen in tourist areas across Thailand. Attacks are most common during full moon parties or similar events, and near bars late at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking, alcohol and assaults"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink spiking and drug-assisted sexual assault does happen in tourist areas around Thailand, with male and female victims. Do not leave your drinks unattended or accept drinks from strangers. Pre-arrange your transport home so you do not have to accept lifts in unlicensed vehicles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinks served in bars are often stronger than those in the UK. Alcohol and drugs can make you less alert and more vulnerable to accidents, injuries, robbery and assaults."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Thailand."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of card fraud. Do not lose sight of your card during transactions. There have been incidents of ATM skimming. Use an ATM in a bank and always protect your PIN."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Job scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be wary of job offers that appear too good to be true. People have arrived in Thailand and been illegally transported to neighbouring countries on the promise of high-paying jobs, which turn out to be scams. When you re-enter Thailand you may then be detained while your immigration status is validated."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["passports confiscated by scammers"]},{"k":"li","s":["victims being held in poor living conditions"]},{"k":"li","s":["coercion into undertaking wider online scamming activity"]},{"k":"li","s":["pressure to make large payments to be released from sham jobs"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy in Bangkok’s video talks about what to be aware of when living or travelling in Thailand:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Facebook – visiting Thailand video","https://www.facebook.com/ukinthailand/videos/2132346856805703/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["X – visiting Thailand video","https://x.com/ukinthailand/status/1002378124200329216"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criticising the Thai monarchy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criticising the Thai monarchy (‘lèse-majesté’) is illegal. The law can be interpreted broadly and carries a long prison sentence. British and Thai journalists, human rights defenders and members of the public have faced charges for making political comments or sharing articles online that could be interpreted as being negative towards the institution of the Thai monarchy. The law also covers any accusations about members of the Thai Royal Family, past and present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Images on social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["Posting images of people drinking alcohol or wearing clothing considered inappropriate can be illegal. Both the person who uploaded the images and the people in them could be fined or imprisoned."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Business and property ownership"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thai authorities have increased enforcement against unlawful business ownership arrangements involving foreign nationals. This includes the use of Thai nationals as ‘nominee’ and majority shareholders, where a foreign national provides the funding for, or exercises control over, a business or property ownership arrangement."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are considering buying property, investing in a business or setting up a company in Thailand, make sure you understand local laws and seek independent legal advice. If you already own a business or have property-related investments in Thailand, consider reviewing your ownership arrangements with a qualified legal adviser to ensure they comply with Thai law. Those found to be operating in breach of Thai business laws may face arrest, fines, deportation or other legal penalties."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Deportation"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 28 August 2026, Thailand introduced new deportation regulations. Foreign nationals may be deported without the need for a criminal conviction if the Thai authorities determine that their conduct is contrary to public order, public morals or the wellbeing of the Thai people. Those who are deported may also face restrictions on returning to Thailand. You should comply with all local laws and regulations and follow instructions issued by Thai authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to fly a drone in Thailand if it is not registered. You must ",["register your drone","https://anyregis.nbtc.go.th/home_member/"]," with Thailand’s National Broadcasting and Telecommunications Commission (NBTC) within 30 days of entering Thailand or purchasing a drone in Thailand even if you do not intend to fly it."]},{"k":"p","s":["The regulations apply to all drones, including those for recreational use. The fine for an unregistered drone with the NBTC is 100,000 baht or five years imprisonment or both."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gambling – playing cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thailand has strict laws on gambling. Under the Playing Cards Act (1943) it is illegal to carry over one hundred and twenty playing cards. Violation of the Act could lead to prosecution, a fine, or even imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police may ask to check your passport. If you do not have it with you, you could be asked to produce it within 24 hours at a police station. Usually, a copy of the photo page of your passport will be sufficient."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to smoke in public with a fine of up to 5,000 Thai baht. It is illegal to possess or use any vape, e-cigarette, pod, e-liquid, or heat-not-burn device in Thailand. Offences can lead to confiscation, heavy fines (typically 5,000–30,000 Thai bhat), detention, and court proceedings. You may be required to remain in Thailand until the case has been finalised. There are no exceptions for tourists or for personal use."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol sale restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The sale of alcohol is restricted between midnight and 11am. This does not apply to licensed hotels, international airport terminals or authorised entertainment venues. Exercise caution when purchasing or consuming alcohol in public places during restricted hours and check with venue owners or shop sellers. Failure to comply could result in a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thailand has strict laws against drug use, possession and trafficking. Possessing small quantities of illegal substances can lead to heavy fines or imprisonment. Possessing ",["Class A drugs","https://www.siam-legal.com/litigation/criminal-defence-drug-offences-in-thailand.php"]," can lead to the death penalty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Conditions in prisons and other detention facilities in Thailand are harsh, with limited access to healthcare. Detainees have died in custody."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some British nationals have suffered severe psychiatric problems because of drug use, sometimes leading to suicide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cannabis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cannabis laws in Thailand are strictly enforced and have changed in recent years. You must follow local regulations on possession, use and export."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cannabis use in Thailand is restricted to medical purposes only. You must not buy, possess or use it without a Thai-issued medical prescription, which is limited to a 30-day supply. Recreational use remains illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take cannabis out of Thailand without the appropriate export permission from the authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attempting to take cannabis out of Thailand will result in penalties, including fines starting at 30,000 Thai baht per kilogram (about £684 per kg). If you do not pay, you will be detained or imprisoned. You will also be placed on an immigration watchlist affecting future travel to Thailand."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cannabis is illegal in many countries. If you carry it when arriving in, or transiting through, another country, you risk arrest and serious penalties, including long prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thailand is generally a safe place for LGBT+ travellers. Thailand legalised same-sex marriage in January 2025. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Elephant treks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Elephant treks can be dangerous, especially if elephants are mistreated or not handled properly. Use a reliable, licensed tour guide. British nationals have been seriously injured and killed because handlers have lost control of the elephant."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming off coastal areas, especially during monsoon season. People have drowned in strong riptides. Thailand has lifeguards on duty at designated beaches and operates a flag system for safe swimming. Follow all warning signs, especially red flags."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jellyfish can swim close to the shore, particularly during the rainy season from May to October. Jellyfish stings can be fatal. Take local advice from your hotel and dive centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming, diving, kayaking or white water rafting in rivers or close to waterfalls, particularly in the rainy season. Currents can be extremely strong."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving schools may have limited resources and do not always observe safety and maintenance standards. Always:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask to see a dive operator’s credentials"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the conditions on your insurance policy – some policies require dive instructors to have certain qualifications"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure safety equipment looks to be in good condition"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure oxygen is available on the boat"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask about safety precautions, including the ability to transfer divers to a hyperbaric chamber"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have not had any previous diving experience, check what to do if something goes wrong, including how to call for help while at sea."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thailand has a high number of road traffic accidents, particularly with motorcycles. The World Health Organisation (WHO) ranks Thailand as one of the world’s deadliest countries for ",["fatalities on motorcycles","https://www.who.int/health-topics/road-safety#tab=tab_1"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Thailand, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You’ll need to carry both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence while driving. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Thailand, you can apply for a Thai driving licence using your UK driving licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Car and motorcycle hire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Motorcycles and scooters for hire in tourist areas are often unregistered and cannot be used legally on a public road. Before you hire a vehicle, make sure your travel insurance covers you and check the small print of the lease agreement, paying particular attention to any limits on engine size and necessary licenses. Many travel insurance policies expect you to hold the correct UK licence for the type of car, motorbike or scooter you intend to drive abroad. This means that if you wouldn’t be legally permitted to drive it in the UK, your insurer may not cover you for driving it in Thailand."]},{"k":"p","s":["By law, you must wear a helmet when riding a motorcycle."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you drive a car or ride a motorcycle in Thailand without a valid licence, it could invalidate your travel insurance and you’ll be unable to claim if you have an accident or injury."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nok Air has been suspended from operating international flights due to safety concerns by Thailand’s Civil Aviation Authority, though still operates domestically within Thailand."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many passenger boat services operating between the mainland and islands. Boats can sink or collide, which has led to fatalities, including of British nationals. Accidents are usually due to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["overloading"]},{"k":"li","s":["poor maintenance"]},{"k":"li","s":["rough seas, particularly during monsoon season"]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainy season"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season is generally from May to October. In Koh Samui and south-east Thailand it is usually from November to March. However, weather patterns have become increasingly unpredictable and periods of intense rainfall can occur across Thailand."]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rainfall can cause flash flooding, landslides and disruption to transport, particularly in northern, north-eastern and mountainous areas. Conditions can change rapidly and may result in road closures and local travel disruption. Lakes, caves and waterfalls are particularly at risk of dangerous flash flooding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local authority advice and monitor the ",["Thai Meteorological Department","https://www.tmd.go.th/en/"]," for weather warnings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes and tremors are a risk in northern Thailand. ",["Earthquake Track","https://earthquaketrack.com/"]," lists recent activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Thailand. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Thailand-Malaysia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to parts of the south, near the Thailand-Malaysia border:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Pattani Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yala Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["Narathiwat Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["The districts of Chana, Thepa, Na Thawi and Saba Yoi in southern Songkhla Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO also advises against all but essential travel on the Hat Yai to Padang Besar train line that runs through these provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to regular attacks in the provinces by the border with Malaysia. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Thailand-Cambodia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["In July 2025, Thailand and Cambodia fought along parts of the border. The fighting included the use of rocket and artillery fire. Tensions remain and fighting erupted again at various points along the border in early December. Land borders and crossings between Thailand and Cambodia continue to be suspended. Some tourist destinations in border areas such as the Khao Phra Wihan/Preah Vihear temple, the Ta Kwai/Ta Krabey temple and the Ta Muen Thom/Tamone Thom temple are closed."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are also unexploded landmines in the border area."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 20km of the land border with Cambodia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Thailand-Laos border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Not all land border crossings into Laos are open to foreign nationals. Even if the border crossing is open, you may need to get a visa for Laos in advance. Check the entry requirements in the ",["Laos travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/laos/entry-requirements"],". Follow the instructions of local authorities and be vigilant in the border areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Thailand-Myanmar border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in Myanmar is unpredictable and liable to change without notice. See ",["Myanmar travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/myanmar"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 191 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local number: 1669"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest information on vaccinations and health risks in ",["TravelHealthPro’s Thailand guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/221/thailand#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Thailand","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/221/thailand"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["rabies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Thailand. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["There can be high levels of air pollution in large cities. This includes Bangkok and Chiang Mai, which are also affected by seasonal regional smoke haze caused by farmers burning trees and crops. The high pollution and ",["particulate count","https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/air-quality-statistics/concentrations-of-particulate-matter-pm10-and-pm25#trends-in-concentrations-of-pm25-in-the-uk-2009-to-2022"]," sometimes reach dangerous levels. This may worsen bronchial, sinus or asthma conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check air quality levels for many cities on the World Air Quality Index website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hospitals and pharmacies across Thailand will usually accept UK prescriptions. Brand-name medication can often be more expensive than locally produced medication."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medication sold on the street may not be genuine or may have been stolen. Taking medication without medical advice or a prescription can have serious health consequences."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Thailand"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Thailand","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/thailand-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["All hospitals require a guarantee of payment before treating patients. Make sure you have adequate health insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private hospitals in Thailand are of a high standard but can be expensive. Public hospitals and clinics do not always meet UK standards, particularly outside Bangkok."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Thailand"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 191 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 1669"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 199"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 191"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist police: 1155"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tourist Police have developed a new application called Thailand Tourist Police to facilitate communication between tourists and our services online. The application is available to tourists who do not have a Thai SIM card. The application features information about tourist attractions and notifications regarding natural disasters or safety concerns in the vicinity of tourists."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?serviceType=lawyers&country=Thailand"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Thailand"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Thailand"]," in Thailand"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Thailand","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-thailand?utm_source=%2Fbritish-embassy-bangkok&utm_medium=Embassy&utm_campaign=Bangkok"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Thailand","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/thailand-prisoner-pack?utm_source=%2Fbritish-embassy-bangkok&utm_medium=Embassy&utm_campaign=Bangkok"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/thailand/british-embassy-bangkok"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/thailand/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Thailand","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-thailand"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":28880,"change":"Updated information about visa requirements for travellers entering Thailand by land or air (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/the-religious-left-may-be-rising-but-black-christian-women-have-been-there-all-along-296110":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"27b35fdbe3f6dcb3b341a11ffc9caf7be54d1ec3f426bf3e5ea50c9df990e656","read":"https://theconversation.com/the-religious-left-may-be-rising-but-black-christian-women-have-been-there-all-along-296110","bytes":188446,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"The ‘religious left’ may be rising – but Black Christian women have been there all along","by":[{"n":"Dara Delgado","r":"Assistant Professor of Religion, University of North Carolina Wilmington"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T17:47:30Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["During campaign season, headlines were full of candidates who spoke openly about their faith – and many of them were Democrats."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Adam Hamilton","https://www.kansascity.com/opinion/opn-columns-blogs/david-hudnall/article317948881.html"],", the new senator-elect from Kansas, is pastor of the United States’ largest United Methodist congregation. ",["Frederick Haynes","https://www.cbsnews.com/texas/news/texas-30-congressional-district-election-results-2026/"],", who will represent a Texas district in the U.S. House of Representatives, is a Baptist pastor. ",["Texas Sen.-elect James Talarico","https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/08/16/senate-hopeful-talarico-touts-his-faith-texas-republicans-call-it-blasphemy/"]," is a Presbyterian seminary student who put a biblical commandment – “Love thy neighbor” – at the center of his campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since election night, journalists and commentators have attributed a significant amount of credit for the proverbial “Blue Wave” ",["to the religious left","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/nx-s1-6029108/how-religion-helped-democrats-win-control-of-congress?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"],". Although some mention Michigan Sen.-elect Abdul El-Sayed, who is Muslim, and Ohio Gov.-elect Amy Acton, who is Jewish, ",["the focus has been on progressive Christians","https://religionnews.com/2026/11/04/on-election-night-the-religious-left-is-back/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As ",["a scholar of race, gender and religion","https://www.uncw.edu/profiles/d/delgadod"]," whose work focuses on ",["Black Protestant Christianity","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=-F1k-RAAAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"],", I found post-election reporting about a rise in the religious left curious. Voters from many faith traditions did help power the “Blue Wave,” but one often-overlooked group has long been the left’s staunchest supporters: Black Christian women."]},{"k":"h","s":["Steady support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Focus on the “return” of the religious Democrats highlights the contrast between the religious diversity on the left and the ",["allegiance between MAGA Republicans and evangelicals on the right","https://www.newsweek.com/white-evangelical-support-for-republicans-ticked-up-despite-blue-tsunami-12672721"],". ",["According to NBC exit polls","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/exit-polls"],", 82% of voters who consider themselves white evangelicals or born-again Christians voted for GOP candidates in 2026. In 2024, 82% of evangelicals in 10 key states ",["voted for President Donald Trump","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-elections/exit-polls"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But talking about religious Democrats as if they are a new, shiny bauble implies that, until this election, religious progressives have been off the ballot. That is simply not the case, especially when it comes to Black women."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Over the last four elections","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-elections/exit-polls/"],", ",["majorities of both female voters","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-elections/exit-polls/"]," ",["and Black voters","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-elections/exit-polls"]," ",["have voted blue","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/exit-polls"],". Black women vote for Democrats ",["by an ever bigger margin","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/exit-polls"],": 93%, in 2026 exit polls, compared with 59% of women overall and 86% of Black men. Although Black women account for only 5-7% of Americans, they have been the most consistent Democratic voting bloc."]},{"k":"p","s":[["More than 7 in 10 Black Americans are Christian","https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2025/12/02/key-facts-about-black-americans-and-religion/"],", and the vast majority are Protestant. Another 4% belong to other faiths, including Islam, and 22% are religiously unaffiliated. According to Pew’s 2023-24 ",["Religious Landscape Survey","https://www.pewresearch.org/religious-landscape-study/religious-tradition/historically-black-protestant/"],", 2 in 3 members of Black Protestant denominations are women."]},{"k":"h","s":["‘God told me to go’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many Black women candidates spoke about faith on the campaign trail."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, ",["Keisha Lance Bottoms","https://www.instagram.com/p/C8I1ZNix5Fq/?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet"],", the governor-elect of Georgia, ",["attends a","https://www.umnews.org/en/news/united-methodists-win-big-in-midterms"]," ",["Methodist church","https://www.instagram.com/reels/DfN5wclxzTq/"],". A few days after her victory, she spoke at the historic ",["Ebenezer Baptist Church","https://www.ebenezeratl.org/our-history/"]," in Atlanta, pastored by Democratic Sen. Raphael Warnock of Georgia. During her visit, Lance Bottoms recalled that ",["she had prayed about whether to run for governor","https://www.wsbtv.com/news/local/atlanta/georgia-election-2026-governor-elect-bottoms-speaks-historic-atlanta-church/HK4Z7JD7UBDSHDHK663RIYIKBU/"]," and said that “God told me to go.” Her billionaire opponent was a “Goliath,” she said, but “ ",["our God supplied all of our needs","https://www.wsbtv.com/news/local/atlanta/georgia-election-2026-governor-elect-bottoms-speaks-historic-atlanta-church/HK4Z7JD7UBDSHDHK663RIYIKBU/"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Anita Earls","https://www.instagram.com/p/DZI9WnYlYDd/?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet"],", who was re-elected as a judge on the North Carolina Supreme Court, is a longtime member of the ",["African Methodist Episcopal Church","https://www.ame-church.com/our-church/our-history/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Among sitting Democrats, Delaware Sen. Lisa Blunt Rochester ",["has spoken about her Christian faith","https://www.christianpost.com/news/lisa-blunt-rochester-details-why-she-prayed-during-capitol-riot.html"],". Massachusetts Rep. ",["Ayanna Pressley","https://religionnews.com/2020/11/04/5-faith-facts-the-squad-omar-tlaib-a-pressley-aoc-muslim-catholic-baptist/"],", who grew up Baptist, has called herself “ ",["a sister in Christ","https://pressley.house.gov/2023/10/20/video-pressley-colleagues-faith-leaders-renew-call-for-ceasefire-to-save-lives/"]," and a woman of faith. Someone who believes in the power of prayer.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Each of these women is part of the religious left."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before them was ",["Shirley Chisholm","https://www.womenshistory.org/education-resources/biographies/shirley-chisholm"],", who became the first Black woman elected to Congress in 1968. Four years later, she was the first Black woman to run for president on the Democratic ticket. Her 1970 memoir, “ ",["Unbought and Unbossed","https://www.harpercollins.com/products/unbought-and-unbossed-shirley-chisholm?variant=40152567545890"],",” recounts her commitment to progressive ideals, ranging from education to women’s reproductive rights, and to her Christian faith."]},{"k":"p","s":["“America has the laws and the material resources it takes to ensure justice for all its people,” ",["she wrote","https://www.harpercollins.com/products/unbought-and-unbossed-shirley-chisholm?variant=40152567545890"],". “What it lacks is the heart, the humanity, the Christian love that it would take. It is perhaps unrealistic to hope that I can help give this nation any of those things, but that is what I believe I have to try to do.”"]},{"k":"h","s":["Long history"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before Black women were voted into office, however, they were already ",["pillars of progressive politics","https://theconversation.com/the-women-who-stood-with-martin-luther-king-jr-and-sustained-a-movement-for-social-change-197262"],". Historically, Black churches have been more than a place to foster belief. They have also been community-based institutions that fostered social, political and economic justice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Within Black denominations, men tend to hold senior leadership positions. In his famed book “ ",["The Souls of Black Folk","https://wwnorton.com/books/9780393870749"],",” sociologist ",["W.E.B. DuBois","https://hutchinscenter.fas.harvard.edu/web-dubois"]," observed that the Black preacher was also a community “leader, a politician, an orator, a ‘boss,’ an intriguer, an idealist.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women’s role was less public, ",["but no less vital","https://search.worldcat.org/title/45024509"],", including social and political organizing. In “ ",["Witnessing and Testifying","https://www.fortresspress.com/store/product/9780800636036/Witnessing-and-Testifying"],",” religion professor ",["Rosetta Ross","https://www.spelman.edu/staff/profiles/rosetta-e-ross.html"]," showed how Black women’s faith and activism inspired each other during the Civil Rights Movement. Among the women Ross surveyed is Ella Baker, who organized the initial meeting for what would become the Student Nonviolent Coordinating Committee and often “used Christian scripture to admonish listeners to fight” for freedom."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women like Baker, ",["voting rights activist Fannie Lou Hamer","https://www.womenshistory.org/education-resources/biographies/fannie-lou-hamer"],", and ",["Clara Muhammad","https://blackwomensreligiousactivism.org/activists/clara-muhammad/"],", wife of Nation of Islam founder Elijah Muhammad, show how Black communities’ concerns and faith ",["often intertwined with progressive politics","https://tupress.temple.edu/books/jesus-jobs-and-justice"],". In 1958, Nannie Helen Burroughs, ",["founder of the Women’s Auxiliary of the National Baptist Convention","https://nationalhumanitiescenter.org/fellows-books/jesus-jobs-and-justice-african-american-women-and-religion/"],", said that African American Christians wanted “ ",["Jesus, jobs and justice","https://tupress.temple.edu/books/jesus-jobs-and-justice"],".”"]},{"k":"h","s":["Black, Christian and progressive"]},{"k":"p","s":["Today, too, faith guides many progressive Black women’s politics and public service. For voting rights activists, for example, casting a ballot ",["is not just a right","https://www.youtube.com/shorts/IkRHSH_fm6E"],", ",["but something sacred","https://www.threads.com/@mspackyetti/post/DfQWAfJGuoB?xmt=AQG0RG5LfTo-19vEzz94McrHxamAYtow3uD9zlIjxYzpxlZ_mc153H6zCkaOgXYzbiTYQjjm&slof=1"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the past week, journalists and political pundits have drawn attention to the many different groups that ",["moved to the left","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/nx-s1-6028080/voter-polls-midterms-demographics"]," to fuel Democrats’ midterm victories, including young voters, Latinos, Asian Americans, men and political independents. Black women voters, meanwhile, ",["have remained steady","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/exit-polls"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indeed, history has shown how ",["their steadiness","https://doi.org/10.1017/S1743923X23000417"]," helped ",["guide the Democratic Party’s","https://www.wnycstudios.org/podcasts/takeaway/segments/black-women-role-democratic-party"]," ",["political and moral compass","https://www.nbcnews.com/news/nbcblk/story-black-women-politics-how-we-got-kamala-harris-ascent-n1236528"],". And I am willing to wager that they will continue to play an essential role in what the left does between now and 2028."]}],"chars":6348}};
